uoted in the paper?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:23e19e25602589efaad70a244b32268c40bfd13aed5ba20ebe40a5abb7978337","title":"How does retaining the light conifold complex-structure field change KKLT vacuum structure, moduli masses, supersymmetry breaking, required localized D3 charge, and soft terms after antibrane uplift?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0049"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:232c80ba392b2322dca8d45d81cd319cdb382c9270c74e8c48000d787a389335","title":"Which integral special Kähler scalar geometries admit quantum-gravity UV completions in ungauged four-dimensional N = 2 vector sectors?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0051"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2354b78d6e59edddc763d0c2c00417cb1b787f65a7fb9bcd16095eb4af5ba9b8","title":"Can canonical quintessence, including an exponential dark-matter interaction, increase the Hubble constant inferred from low-redshift observations relative to ΛCDM? The question concerns fitted expansion histories and their statistical fit, motivated by the disagreement between local and CMB-based H0 determinations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:23967e314a0ff22e27a2d33ee7e6189373a7f0be5f2ed32676b1ae0752f0234e","title":"How can gravitational fine-grained entropy methods compute Hawking-radiation entropy consistently with unitary evaporation, despite the growing entropy obtained from the semiclassical radiation state?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0054"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:23e1a2af3f8e0a667ab82f08f7c917e3a4b8ac0e2c442c121177cc97c33b1e93","title":"Can a nonsingular Cuscuton bounce generate nearly scale-invariant scalar seeds without an 